<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $6.0 bln in Dec 30 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $6.0 bln in Dec 30 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $6.0 billion in the December 30 week to $3,824.7 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $2.0 billion to $4,895.9 billion. M-1 rose $600 million to $1,079.1 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,825.2 billion versus $3,822.3 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
